    - target: {fileID: 1253161411824071964, guid: 50fe8fa53408c3d45b668daabee7b142, type: 3}
      propertyPath: m_text
      value: "A streamline is a curve tangent to the flow field everywhere. Intuitively,
        a streamline is the path that a massless particle (The ink) will follow if
        released in a laminar flow field. \r\nFor example, if a small shape is placed
        into a water flow path, and assuming the water flow does not change over
        time (i.e., laminar flow), the trajectory of the shape is a streamline.\r"
      objectReference: {fileID: 0}
